Inspired by a recent thread, in which an unspoiled player wishes for a
+3 hat (a perfectly reasonable early wish, imho).

I'm spoiled rotten, nethack-wise. However it wasn't always so: I can't
remember when I read my first spoiler, but I do know there was a
significant period when I had only the guidebook and my own feeble wits
to keep me alive in the dungeon. Needless to say, I never survived very
long.

My first ever wish (water demon, probably) happened to occur in this
period, and remember taking a long while to think about it, then asking
for a floating eye corpse, since that was the most useful thing I had
encountered in my previous games. Not a bad wish, I would say. Come to
think of it, I've a feeling it was not knowing what to wish for was
that inspired my first ever spoil.

So here's the thread's question: Do you remember your first ever wish?
Was it from a \,/,( or &? Were you unspoiled at the time? Did you ask
for something you'd already seen in nethack, or something you'd only
read about or guessed at?


